### Step 4: Querying Available Time Slots

To efficiently query available time slots for a specific service on a given date, you can use the following query in Laravel:

```php
use App\Models\Appointment;
use App\Models\Schedule;
use App\Models\Break as BreakModel;
use App\Models\Holiday;

$serviceId = 1; // Example service ID
$targetDate = now()->startOfDay(); // Example target date

// Get business hours and breaks for the target day
$schedule = Schedule::where('service_id', $serviceId)
    ->where('day_of_week', $targetDate->format('l'))
    ->first();

// Get breaks for the schedule
$breaks = BreakModel::where('schedule_id', $schedule->id)->get();

// Get holidays for the service
$holidays = Holiday::where('service_id', $serviceId)
    ->where(function ($query) use ($targetDate) {
        $query->where('start_date', '<=', $targetDate)
              ->where('end_date', '>=', $targetDate);
    })->get();

// Get appointments for the service on the target date
$appointments = Appointment::where('service_id', $serviceId)
    ->whereDate('appointment_time', $targetDate->toDateString())
    ->get();

// Determine available slots
$availableSlots = [];
$currentTime = $schedule->start_time;
while ($currentTime < $schedule->end_time) {
    if (!$holidays->isEmpty() || !$breaks->isEmpty()) {
        // Check if current time is within breaks or holidays
        if ($breaks->contains(function ($break) use ($currentTime) {
            return $currentTime >= $break->start_time && $currentTime <= $break->end_time;
        })) {
            $currentTime = (clone $currentTime)->addMinutes(1);
            continue;
        }

        if ($holidays->contains(function ($holiday) use ($targetDate) {
            return $targetDate->gte($holiday->start_date) && $targetDate->lte($holiday->end_date);
        })) {
            $currentTime = (clone $currentTime)->addMinutes(1);
            continue;
        }
    }

    // Check if the slot is already booked
    if (!$appointments->contains(function ($appointment) use ($currentTime) {
        return $appointment->appointment_time->toTimeString() == $currentTime->toTimeString();
    })) {
        $availableSlots[] = $currentTime;
    }

    // Move to the next available slot
    $currentTime = (clone $currentTime)->addMinutes(30); // Assuming slots are every 30 minutes
}

return $availableSlots;
```

This query checks for available time slots by considering business hours, breaks, holidays, and existing appointments. It ensures that you have an efficient way to find available slots for a specific service on a given date.

